  "notes": [
    "Hand-assembled, not generated by `tubuild.py create`: tu_map cannot segment arm9/main, so there was no candidate id to create from. The schema follows the arm9/ActorDerived entry, which took the same route.",
    "func_02017278 is the class's real constructor: it writes the whole dFader_c -> dFdBrightness_c -> dFdColor_c -> dFdDummy_c vptr chain and the inherited field stores, i.e. the complete-object ctor with every base sub-object ctor inlined (all bases carry inline ctors in their headers). It is folded as the real member `dFdDummy_c::dFdDummy_c()`, the symbols.txt row is renamed to _ZN10dFdDummy_cC1Ev, and the sole caller src/d_s_dsmt.c is respelled to the mangled name in the same change.",
    "The mangled `_ZN8dFader_c13AdvanceInterpEv` extern each AdvanceFade shard used becomes the inherited member call `AdvanceInterp()` -- same target, same bytes.",
    "dFader_c::D0 remains the family's one non-matching body and keeps its shard; dFader_c::D1 keeps its own entry past the D0 hole because delinks grants a file exactly one contiguous range."
